.TH RECVFROM 2
.SH NAME
recvfrom \- receive one local datagram
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.PP
.B long recvfrom(int fd, void *buf, unsigned long len, int flags, struct sockaddr *addr, unsigned int *addrlen);
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives one queued AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM message. The message boundary is
preserved and a short buffer truncates the returned message. An empty queue
parks on the native AIO ring; close and shutdown wake parked operations.
.SH ERRORS
EFAULT denotes malformed user buffers or address storage.
